     "note": "Sparkline — a trend in one line, kept light. Braille dots or low blocks —",
     "body": "# Sparkline — a trend in one line, kept light. Braille dots or low blocks —\n# never the full block █ (it reads as a heavy slab).\n\n## families — pick by how much resolution the line has earned\n braille line   ⡠⠔⠒⠊⠉⠉⠑⠢⠤⠄⠂⠁⠂⠄⠢     finest, airy (2×4 dots per cell)\n braille fill   ⣀⣄⣆⣇⣧⣶⣷⣿⣿⣷⣧⣇⣆⣄⣀     a filled area, still not a slab\n low blocks     ▁▂▃▄▅▆▇▆▅▄▃▂▁▂▄▆       eight steps, universally installed\n dots           ․˳•˚°˚•˳․˳•˚°˚•˳       a whisper — for a line that is context\n bars           ⡇⡆⡄⡀⡄⡆⡇⣇⣧⣶⣷⣿         column-per-sample, when count is small\n\n## anchored — a line without a scale is decoration\n cpu    ▁▂▄▃▅▆▇▆▄▃  42%        latest value printed, right-aligned\n cpu    ▁▂▄▃▅▆▇▆▄▃  42% ▲6     with the delta against the previous window\n cpu  0┤▁▂▄▃▅▆▇▆▄▃├100         an explicit floor and ceiling\n cpu    ▁▂▄▃▅▆▇▆▄▃  ⌃92 ⌄11    the window's own high and low\n\n## marked — one sample matters more than the run\n p99    ▁▂▄▃▅▆▇▆▄▃             a plain run\n p99    ▁▂▄▃▅▆◆▆▄▃             ◆ on the peak — the subject of the sentence\n p99    ▁▂▄▃▅▆▇▆▄▃ ╌╌╌ 200ms   a threshold as a dashed line, never a band\n err    ▁▁▁▂▁▁▇▁▁▁             the one spike is the only coloured cell\n\n## stacked — several metrics share one label column\n cpu    ▁▂▄▃▅▆▇▆▄▃   42%\n mem    ▃▃▄▄▄▅▅▅▆▆   61%\n net    ▁▁▂▁▄▁▁▂▁▁    3%\n ↑ one width for every row: a sparkline column that does not align is a mess\n\n# paint: the run -> kin-1 (gilding) or bone-2 · a real spike -> aka-0\n# label left and dim, value right and bone; fixed width, always"
