     "body": "# Numeric table — when a chart would lose the exact values. Columns align on\n# the decimal point, not on the left edge.\n\n## the plain form — no vertical rules, one hairline under the head\n metric        now      1h ago     24h      trend\n ────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n requests    18,402     17,908   402,118   ▁▂▄▃▅▆▇\n p50 (ms)        42         44        41   ▃▃▂▃▂▂▁\n p99 (ms)       486        198       211   ▁▁▂▂▃▅▇   ⚠\n errors        0.31%      0.08%     0.12%  ▁▁▁▂▁▁▇   ✗\n ────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n ↑ numbers right, labels left, units in the header — never repeated per cell\n\n## with a delta column, signed and aligned\n revenue     ¥ 1.24M    ▲  +8.2%\n orders          318    ▲  +2.6%\n refunds        2.1%    ▲  +0.4%   ⚠   up is bad here, so it is marked\n aov         ¥ 3,899    ▼  −5.4%\n ↑ ▲ is not \"good\". The arrow states direction; the mark states judgement.\n\n## grouped rows — one blank line, never a nested box\n edge\n   tokyo      4,820     ▰▰▰▰▰▰▰▰▰▰\n   osaka      3,140     ▰▰▰▰▰▰\n   kyoto      1,890     ▰▰▰▰\n\n origin\n   tokyo      2,204     ▰▰▰▰\n   frankfurt    980     ▰▰\n\n## a wide table that must not wrap — drop columns, never shrink the font\n full      name · region · status · p50 · p99 · errors · last deploy\n narrow    name · status · p99 · errors\n tight     name · p99\n ↑ decide the drop order once and write it down; a table that drops a\n   different column each render is unreadable across two runs\n\n## totals — separated by a rule, never bolded into the body\n ────────────────────────────────────────\n total       9,850     ▰▰▰▰▰▰▰▰▰▰▰▰▰▰▰▰\n\n# paint: head -> text.muted, uppercase, letterspaced · body numbers -> bone-1\n# a value past its threshold -> kaki-1 · past critical -> aka-0\n# rules -> line-0 · trend columns -> kin-1 · never a fill behind a row"
