     "name": "scatter",
     "note": "Scatter — two variables, one point each. Braille gives 2×4 dots per cell,",
     "body": "# Scatter — two variables, one point each. Braille gives 2×4 dots per cell,\n# which is the only way a terminal gets a real point cloud.\n\n## the plain cloud\n latency (ms)\n  500┤                                    ⢀\n     │                                 ⢀⡠⠊\n  250┤                          ⢀⡠⠔⠊⠉\n     │                  ⢀⣀⡠⠤⠒⠉\n  100┤        ⢀⣀⡠⠤⠒⠊⠉\n     │⣀⡠⠤⠒⠉\n    0└────┬────┬────┬────┬────┬────┬────┬─\n         100  200  300  400  500  600  700\n                    concurrency\n\n## with a fit line, and the residual left visible\n     │        ⢀⠔  ⠁\n     │     ⢀⠔⠁ ⠐\n     │  ⢀⠔⠁⠠\n     │⠔⠁ ⠈\n     └───────────────\n ↑ the fit is a line, the points are dots; if they render in the same weight\n   the chart shows one thing instead of two\n\n## the outlier is the story\n     │                                     ◆   ← 2.4s, api-07\n     │\n     │⣀⡠⠤⠒⠊⠉⠉⠑⠒⠤⢄⣀\n     └───────────────────────────────────────\n ↑ one point earns a glyph, a colour and a label. The rest stay dots.\n\n## small multiples — the same axes, repeated\n   web            api            db\n  ┤ ⢀⡠⠔⠊         ┤   ⢀⡠⠔⠒        ┤⠉⠑⠢⢄⡀\n  ┤⠊             ┤⠔⠁             ┤     ⠉⠢⢄\n  └────────      └────────       └────────\n ↑ identical scales, always. Three panels with three scales is three charts\n   pretending to be a comparison.\n\n# paint: points -> bone-2 · a fit or trend line -> kin-1 · the outlier -> aka-0\n# axes, ticks and the frame -> line-0 · axis labels mono and dim"
