     "name": "kpi",
     "note": "Big number — one figure that a person is actually looking for. It gets the",
     "body": "# Big number — one figure that a person is actually looking for. It gets the\n# size; everything else on the card is context for it.\n\n## the card — figure, delta, trend, in that order\n ╭─ revenue · this month ────────────╮\n │                                   │\n │   ¥ 1,240,800                     │\n │   ▲ 8.2%  vs last month           │\n │   ▁▂▄▃▅▆▇  30d                    │\n ╰───────────────────────────────────╯\n\n## a row of them — one scale, one width, one baseline\n revenue        orders         refunds        p99\n ¥ 1.24M        318            2.1%           486 ms\n ▲ 8.2%         ▲ 2.6%         ▲ 0.4%  ⚠      ▲ 121%  ✗\n ▁▂▄▃▅▆▇        ▂▃▃▅▄▆▇        ▁▁▂▂▃▄▅        ▁▁▂▂▃▅▇\n\n## the figure alone, when the context is in the heading\n      18,402\n      requests · last hour\n\n## with its target — the only time a second number may be as large\n      68%        of  100%       error budget spent\n      ▰▰▰▰▰▰▰▱▱▱                9 days left\n\n## states a big number has to be able to say\n      ¥ 1.24M          a value\n      —                no data yet (an em dash, never a zero)\n      0                actually zero (which is a fact, not an absence)\n      ¥ 1.24M ⟳        stale, refreshing\n      ✗ unavailable    the query failed — never show the last good number\n                       without saying that is what you are looking at\n\n# paint: the figure -> text.heading at 2–3× body · the unit -> text.muted\n# the delta arrow states direction only; the ⚠ / ✗ mark states judgement\n# the trend -> kin-1 · never put the figure itself in a trigger colour unless\n# the thing it measures is actually in alarm"
