     "body": "# Lists — the most common block in the language, and the easiest to get wrong.\n# The marker states the kind of list. Pick it once and hold it.\n\n## unordered — order does not matter\n · lacquer, bone and gold\n · two triggers, spent only on events\n · one source, thirteen targets\n ↑ a middle dot, not a bullet: • is a hole punched in the line\n\n## ordered — order is the information\n 1.  read the philosophy\n 2.  lift the palette\n 3.  paste one prompt module\n ↑ numbers right-aligned past nine, or 9. and 10. will not line up\n\n## a ladder — order AND precedence\n 1  rarity beats taste\n 2  meaning beats preference\n 3  legibility beats atmosphere\n ↑ no full stop: this is a rank, not a sentence\n\n## checklist — a thing a person is going to do\n ✓ palette resolved\n ✓ contrast proven\n ▫ themes baked\n ▫ site rebuilt\n ↑ ▫ is empty, not ✗: not-yet-done is not failure\n\n## definition — a term and what it means\n token     a raw value with a stated job\n role      the contract you consume — text.body, action.edge\n target    a program the palette is baked for\n ↑ this is a key-value column; see kv.txt if the values grow\n\n## nested — two levels, and there is no third\n canon/\n   · palette     tokens, roles, the proof\n   · components  the anatomy of a control\n library/\n   · web         the drop-in kit\n   · themes      thirteen programs\n ↑ a third level means the outline is the document. Split the page instead.\n\n## inline — a list inside a sentence\n kitty, foot, alacritty, ghostty and wezterm\n ↑ commas, and one \"and\". Not middle dots, which are for pairs, not prose.\n\n## a run of pairs on one line\n stable · v1.2.0 · MIT · 42 tokens\n\n## what a list must not do\n ✗  a marker per line that changes halfway down\n ✗  a one-item list                      that is a sentence\n ✗  a list of full paragraphs            that is prose with bullets stapled on\n ✗  bold on every item                   then bold means nothing\n\n# paint: markers -> text.gold (·, numbers, ✓) · ▫ and skipped -> text.ghost\n#        terms in a definition list -> text.muted · bodies -> bone"
