     "body": "# Key-value — aligned pairs. Keys dim, values bone; the column is the rhythm.\n\n## the plain column\n unit      web-01\n status    ● up\n uptime    99.7%\n region    eu-central\n\n## with a field marker, in a denser card\n ⟥ commits   86      (+18%)\n ⟥ focus     3 / 12\n\n## leader dots — when the gap grows wide enough to lose the eye\n build ·············· 11.9 s\n tests ··············  1,820 ok\n bundle ············· 214 kB\n ↑ dots only past about 24 columns. Under that they are noise.\n\n## inline — a run of pairs on one line\n branch main · commit 8f2a1c4 · 214 files · 0.4s\n ↑ middle dots, not commas: a comma reads as one sentence, a dot as one list\n\n## two columns, when the pairs are short and many\n os      ubuntu 24.04       cpu     4 vCPU\n kernel  6.8.0-41           mem     8 GB\n arch    aarch64            disk    80 GB\n\n## grouped — a blank line, never a nested box\n identity\n   name     yoshiki\n   version  1.2.0\n   licence  MIT\n\n build\n   themes   13\n   tokens   42\n   checks   184\n\n## values that are not values\n last deploy   —              never happened (an em dash, not \"null\")\n owner         unassigned     a real state, said in words\n p99           ⟳              still measuring\n region        ✗ unreachable  the lookup failed, and says so\n\n## long values — wrap under the value column, never under the key\n error     connection reset by peer after 30s; the upstream\n           closed before any byte of the body arrived\n\n# paint: keys -> text.muted · values -> bone-1 · ⟥ and leader dots -> gold\n#        deltas (+n) -> ok.text · align every value to one left edge"
