     "name": "banners",
     "note": "Banners — section openers and headers. One heavy rule per screen; everything",
     "body": "# Banners — section openers and headers. One heavy rule per screen; everything\n# else is light. A page with two heavy banners has no hierarchy, only weight.\n\n## rules, by weight\n ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━   heavy — once per screen\n ─────────────────────────────────────────────────   light — between blocks\n ╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌   dashed — an aside\n\n## the openers\n ⧉  S E C T I O N                              marker opener — data blocks\n [ Section ]                                   bracket title — settings, groups\n ◇ ─────────────  title  ───────────── ◇       centered ceremonial\n ── 01 · the one law ─────────────────────     numbered, for a document\n ❯ section                                     prompt opener — CLI output\n\n## the capsule — a calm page's heading\n ╭──────────────────────────────────────────╮\n │  ◆   t i t l e                           │\n ╰──────────────────────────────────────────╯\n\n## the titled rule — a heading that is also a divider\n ╭─ palette ─────────────────────────────────\n │  tokens, roles, and the proof\n ╰╴\n\n## with a status on the right — the shape a build banner wants\n ╭─ ◆ ─ deploy ─  main  ✓ clean ─ v1.2 ──────╮\n ╰───────────────────────────────────────────╯\n\n## a document header — the block at the top of a file\n ════════════════════════════════════════════════\n  yoshiki · palette\n  the single source; everything downstream is baked\n ════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\n## a comment-block header, for source files\n /* ════════════════════════════════════════════\n    build.py — one palette in, thirteen targets out\n    ════════════════════════════════════════════ */\n\n## sizes — pick by how much of the page the section owns\n a page       the capsule, or the heavy rule\n a section    the numbered rule, or ⧉ S E C T I O N\n a block      [ Section ] or the titled rule\n a paragraph  a light rule, or nothing at all\n\n## what a banner must not do\n ✗  a heavy rule above and below the same title     it is a heading, not a cage\n ✗  a banner wider than the content under it\n ✗  ASCII art as a heading in a must-read path      it does not survive a diff\n ✗  two ceremonial openers on one screen\n\n# paint: rules and frames -> border.hairline · the accent glyph -> text.gold\n#        the title -> text.heading · any status on the rule -> its own role"
