     "name": "nameplates",
     "note": "Nameplates — spaced capitals between paired marks.",
     "body": "# Nameplates — spaced capitals between paired marks.\n# Lift a line; replace the word. One nameplate per surface — it is a seal,\n# not a watermark.\n\n·  A U R O R A  ·                    quiet — default\n—  A U R O R A  —                    formal\n⟦  A U R O R A  ⟧                    technical / HUD\n◇  A U R O R A  ◇                    ceremonial\n◸  A U R O R A  ◿                    framed / poster\n\n# Why spaced caps read as a brand, not a word: wide tracking stops the eye\n# from parsing language and makes it read a mark instead. Keep tracking at\n# >= 2 spaces between letters; pair the sigils.\n\n# Optional, dosed: a single accent glyph may seal a plate — never more\n# than one, and only where it earns its place.\n◇  A U R O R A  ✦  ◇"
