     "note": "Dividers & markers — by weight and role. Heavy once per screen, light freely.",
     "body": "# Dividers & markers — by weight and role. Heavy once per screen, light freely.\n# Plain UTF-8, monospace- and wrap-safe. Color the rule border.hairline,\n# any accent glyph text.gold.\n\n## between — separate sibling blocks\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━   heavy — chapter / hard break (one per screen)\n─────────────────────────────   light — paragraph / soft break\n╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌   dashed — an aside, a quieter break\n· · · · · · · · · · · · · · ·   dotted — a whisper between lines\n───────────── ◆ ─────────────   accented — a seam with one mark (ceremonial)\n─ ─ ─ ─ ─ ─ ─ ─ ─ ─ ─ ─ ─ ─ ─   spaced — airy, generous\n\n## open — start of a region (weight at the top)\n╭─                              soft opener — a roof begins\n┌╴                              sharp opener — a built edge begins\n◆ ─────────────                mark + rule — a titled start\n╭─ ◆ ─ TITLE ───                opener with an inline mark and label\n\n## end — close of information (the \"no more below\" mark)\n───────────────╴                a line that stops short — info ends, it breathes\n╰╴                              soft terminator — the roof comes down\n╰───────────────                open close — left holds, right lets go\n· · ·                           trailing rest — more was possible, none follows\n─────── ◆                       rule into a final mark — sealed end\n   ╶─ end ─╴                     labelled stop, when it must be explicit\n\n## inline — within a line\n ·    middle dot — tight separator (key · value)\n │    bar — segment divider (a │ b │ c)\n —    dash — pause / range\n →    leads-to (input → output)\n\n# Rule: an opener and its end should rhyme — a soft ╭─ closes with ╰╴,\n# a sharp ┌╴ closes with ╶┘. Don't open round and end hard on the same block."
