     "body": "# Callouts — a flagged line, colour by role. No box: the mark is the category.\n# Verdict glyph, short label, one clause. The same five everywhere.\n\n## the five\n ✓ ok      build passed · 46 tokens synced\n ⚠ warn    cache expires in two hours\n ✗ error   seal mismatch — cannot continue\n ⧉ note    information lives in tone, not in blue\n → tip     paste one prompt module, stack the rest\n\n## without the label, when the glyph is unambiguous in context\n ✓ 1,820 tests passed\n ⚠ 3 deprecated tokens still referenced\n ✗ contrast floor missed: text.ghost on bg.hover — 2.9:1\n\n## with a cause and a way out — the shape an error actually owes you\n ✗ error   build failed\n           ↳ canon/palette/washi: kin-2 on ink-3 is 4.33:1, floor is 4.5\n           ↳ raise kin-2, or drop text.gold-dim from the proof\n\n## indented under the thing it is about\n palette.yml\n   ✓ 42 tokens resolved\n   ⚠ 2 tokens declared but never used by a role\n themes/\n   ✓ 13 targets written\n\n## a block callout, when one clause is genuinely not enough\n ⧉ note\n   A custom property resolves where it is DECLARED, not where it is used.\n   A nested [data-theme] scope therefore has to re-declare the whole role\n   contract — inheriting half of it is the bug that looks like a theme bug.\n\n## in a changelog or a README, where it has to survive plain text\n > **⚠ breaking** — `--y-radius` is now `--y-r-card`. One rename, no shim.\n\n## what a callout must not do\n ✗  a box around every line               five boxes is a stack, not a flag\n ✗  ⚠ used for anything you want noticed  then nothing is a warning\n ✗  three callouts in a row               that is a list; write it as one\n ✗  a callout with no subject             \"⚠ something went wrong\" is noise\n\n# paint: ✓ -> ok.text (moss) · ⚠ -> warn.text (persimmon) · ✗ -> danger.text\n#        ⧉ note / → tip -> text.gold or bone · label -> dim, clause -> bone\n#        the ↳ continuation lines -> text.muted, never the trigger colour again"
