     "body": "# Badges — compact status tags, one role-colour each. Pill or brackets.\n\n## the pill — a badge that is an object\n ◆ PRIMARY     ● ACTIVE     ✗ CRITICAL     ✦ AI     v1.0.0     beta\n\n## the bracket — when a pill is too much\n [ primary ]   ( active )   v1.0.0   · ai\n\n## the bare mark — when the row already says what it is\n ◆ primary     ● active     ✗ critical     ○ idle     ◇ queued\n\n## by what the badge is actually saying\n state       ● live      ◐ degraded   ○ idle      ✗ down      ⟳ restarting\n lifecycle   ◆ stable    ◇ beta       ▵ alpha     ⌁ experimental   ⊘ deprecated\n verdict     ✓ passing   ⚠ flaky      ✗ failing   ⋯ pending   ⊝ skipped\n size        ▪ xs        ▪▪ s         ▪▪▪ m       ▪▪▪▪ l\n kind        ⧉ note      → tip        ⚑ breaking  ✦ ai        ⌂ internal\n\n## versions and counts — the quiet ones, and there are always more of them\n v1.2.0    v1.2.0-rc.1    #1421    12 open    3 / 12    +18%\n\n## a row of them — the accent comes last, so the eye lands on it\n web-01   ubuntu 24.04   4 vCPU   ● live\n web-02   ubuntu 24.04   4 vCPU   ✗ down\n\n## in a heading, where a badge is a subtitle\n yoshiki  ◆ stable   v1.2.0   MIT\n\n## what a badge must not do\n ✗  [ NEW ] [ HOT ] [ SALE ] [ ⚡ FAST ]    four accents, so no accent\n ✗  ● ACTIVE in scarlet                     the colour must match the word\n ✗  a badge longer than its row's label     then it is a sentence, write it\n\n# paint: PRIMARY -> gold · ACTIVE -> moss · CRITICAL -> scarlet · AI -> wisteria\n#        DEGRADED / FLAKY -> persimmon · deprecated, skipped, idle -> text.ghost\n#        version and neutral tags -> bone-3 on ink-2\n#        one accent badge per row. Two accents is a decoration, not a status."
