     "note": "Glyph sets — curated rows by meaning. One glyph, one job.",
     "body": "# Glyph sets — curated rows by meaning. One glyph, one job.\n# Pick from a row; never reuse a glyph for two meanings on one screen.\n\n## by meaning\n status     ✓ ✗ ● ○ ◉ ◌ ⊘ ⏻ ⟳ ↺ ◐ ▫ ⋯\n verdict    ✓ ⚠ ✗ ⊝ ⋯                    passed · flaky · failed · skipped · pending\n flow       → ← ↑ ↓ ↦ ↻ ⇄ ⇅ » « ↳ ⤷\n rank       ◆ ◇ ◈ ▲ ▼ ★ ☆ ⬡ ⬢ ▵ ▪\n field      · — │ ┃ ┊ ┆ ╌ ┄\n sigil      ⧉ ⛬ ⊙ ◷ ❖ ⌁ ⌂ ✦ ⚑\n bracket    [ ] ( ) ⟨ ⟩ « » ⟦ ⟧ ◸ ◿\n corner     ╭ ╮ ╰ ╯ ┌ ┐ └ ┘ ╔ ╗ ╚ ╝\n join       ├ ┤ ┬ ┴ ┼ ╞ ╡\n fill       ▰ ▱ ░ ▒ ▓ ▁ ▂ ▃ ▄ ▅ ▆ ▇\n spinner    ⠋ ⠙ ⠹ ⠸ ⠼ ⠴ ⠦ ⠧ ⠇ ⠏         braille, for live ticks\n braille    ⠀ ⡀ ⡄ ⡆ ⡇ ⣇ ⣧ ⣷ ⣿           a density ramp, eight steps\n\n## the pairs that must not be mixed\n ✓ / ✗      verdict          ●  / ○     state\n ▲ / ▼      direction        ⚠         judgement\n ↑ ▲ is not \"good\" and ● is not \"passed\". A glyph that carries two meanings\n   on one screen carries neither.\n\n## tiers — pick the lowest that does the job\n tier 0    ✓ ✗ ● ◆ → ▲ ▼ · — │ ⧉        any font, anywhere, no exceptions\n tier 1    ◇ ○ ◉ ⟳ ↻ ⊘ ★ ▰ ▱ ╭ ╰ ┤      common Unicode, safe in practice\n tier 2    ⣿ ⠋ ⛬ ◷ ❖ ⌁ ⟦ ◸              Nerd Font or a rich terminal —\n                                          never on a must-read path\n Box-drawing and braille are the safest of all: terminals draw them\n programmatically, so they align whatever the font.\n\n## what to reach for, by the question being answered\n did it work?           ✓ ⚠ ✗\n is it on?              ● ○ ◐\n is it working now?     ⟳ ⠹ ⋯\n which way?             → ↑ ▲ ▼\n how important?         ◆ ◇ ·\n where does it go?      ↳ ⤷ »\n is this a warning?     ⚠            and nothing else, ever\n\n## what a glyph must not do\n ✗  an emoji in a must-read line       width is unpredictable, colour is not yours\n ✗  three glyphs on one line           one per line, two at most in a whole row\n ✗  a glyph instead of a word          \"✓\" alone is not \"build passed\"\n ✗  a tier-2 glyph in an error message  the one line that must always render\n\n# paint: verdict glyphs -> their own role colour (ok · warn · danger)\n#        marks, sigils and frames -> text.gold or border.hairline\n#        field and flow glyphs -> text.muted — they are punctuation, not signal"
